("The Bohr effect describes the:","Lower oxygen affinity of haemoglobin at high CO2 and H+",["Greater CO2 carriage by deoxygenated blood","Left shift caused by fetal haemoglobin","Effect of carbon monoxide on haemoglobin"],"It favours oxygen release in metabolically active tissues."),
("The Haldane effect states that:","Deoxygenated blood carries more CO2",["Oxygenated blood carries more CO2","CO2 lowers oxygen affinity","CO2 is carried mainly as carbamino compounds"],"Deoxyhaemoglobin binds H+ and CO2 more readily."),
